# Technical Proposal: CharityML — Finding Donors Predictor

> **Author:** mariam ahmed elghazaly  
> **Date:** April 6, 2026  
> **Project:** Machine Learning — Supervised Learning   

---

## 1. Executive Summary

The **CharityML Finding Donors Predictor** is a supervised machine learning project that predicts whether an individual earns more than $50,000/year using U.S. Census data. The system currently features a modular Python codebase, three custom-built classifiers (Random Forest, Logistic Regression, Gradient Boosting), and a Tkinter desktop GUI for interactive predictions.

This proposal outlines the current state of the project, identifies technical gaps, and presents a phased roadmap for elevating the project to production quality.

---

## 2. Current Architecture

### 2.1 Project Structure

```
finding_donors/
├── finding_donors_gui.py    # Entry point — launches Tkinter GUI
├── app_gui.py               # GUI application (961 lines) — 3-panel layout
├── models.py                # 3 custom ML classifiers (189 lines)
├── data_utils.py            # Synthetic data generation & preprocessing (106 lines)
├── constants.py             # Feature options, color palette, defaults (88 lines)
├── visuals.py               # Matplotlib visualization helpers (146 lines)
├── finding_donors.ipynb     # Jupyter notebook analysis
├── census.csv               # UCI Census dataset (~5.4 MB, ~32,561 records)
├── project_description.md   # Udacity project brief
└── README.md                # Project documentation
```

