## 3. Technical Analysis & Identified Gaps

### 3.1 Data Pipeline


- [data_utils.py](file:///c:/Users/zbook%20g6/machinelearning/Machine_Learning_project/P2/finding_donors/data_utils.py) generates random data with a hardcoded label-scoring heuristic (lines 42-49), rather than loading the real UCI Census dataset.
- The "Browse" button in the GUI calls `_browse_file()` but ultimately invokes `_load_dataset()` which ignores the selected file and generates synthetic data instead (lines 608-619 of [app_gui.py](file:///c:/Users/zbook%20g6/machinelearning/Machine_Learning_project/P2/finding_donors/app_gui.py)).

### 3.2 Machine Learning Models


| Model | Issue |
|-------|-------|
| `SimpleRandomForest` | Single-feature, single-split trees — not real decision trees. More like bagged decision stumps. |
| `SimpleLogisticRegression` | Vanilla gradient descent without regularization; no convergence check. |
| `SimpleGradientBoosting` | Same single-feature/single-split limitation as Random Forest. Residual update loop is O(n) per tree. |

**Reported accuracy** :
- Logistic Regression: 71.87%
- Random Forest: 64.40%
- Gradient Boosting: 72.01%

These are modest results, partially due to the simplified model implementations and the synthetic data distribution.

### 3.4 GUI & UX Issues

- **`visuals.py`** uses `get_ipython()` at module load time (line 9), making it crash when imported outside Jupyter. This file is only usable from the notebook.
- The GUI file is ~960 lines — while modularized from the original 1400-line script, the `CharityMLApp` class still handles data loading, model training, prediction, and all UI rendering in a single class.
- No error handling for edge cases (e.g., predicting before loading data works but feature scaling may fail).

### 3.5 Code Quality

| Issue | Location |
|-------|----------|
| Arabic inline comments mixed with English | `data_utils.py`, `app_gui.py` |
| `visuals.py` has IPython dependency at import time | `visuals.py:8-9` |
| No `requirements.txt` or `pyproject.toml` | Root directory |
| No unit tests | Entire project |
| No `.gitignore` for `.venv`, `__pycache__` | Root directory |
| Duplicate virtual environments | `.venv` and `.venv-1` both exist |

