### Phase 1: Real Data Pipeline (Est. 2 days)

**Goal:** Replace synthetic data with real `census.csv` loading and proper preprocessing.

#### [MODIFY] [data_utils.py](file:///c:/Users/zbook%20g6/machinelearning/Machine_Learning_project/P2/finding_donors/data_utils.py)
- Add `load_census_data(filepath)` function using `pandas.read_csv()`
- Implement proper one-hot encoding for categorical features (or ordinal encoding for tree-based models)
- Add log-transform for skewed features (`capital-gain`, `capital-loss`)
- Implement train/test split using proper stratification
- Keep `generate_synthetic_data()` as a fallback for demo mode

#### [MODIFY] [app_gui.py](file:///c:/Users/zbook%20g6/machinelearning/Machine_Learning_project/P2/finding_donors/app_gui.py)
- Wire up `_browse_file()` to actually load the selected CSV
- Add CSV validation (check expected columns, handle missing values)
- Display real dataset statistics (income distribution, feature summaries)

#### [NEW] requirements.txt
```
numpy>=1.21.0
pandas>=1.3.0
matplotlib>=3.5.0
scikit-learn>=1.0.0
mlflow>=2.0.0
```

---

### Phase 2: Production-Grade ML Models (Est. 3 days)

**Goal:** Replace simplified custom classifiers with scikit-learn implementations for production-quality accuracy.

#### [MODIFY] [models.py](file:///c:/Users/zbook%20g6/machinelearning/Machine_Learning_project/P2/finding_donors/models.py)
- Replace `SimpleRandomForest` → `sklearn.ensemble.RandomForestClassifier`
- Replace `SimpleLogisticRegression` → `sklearn.linear_model.LogisticRegression`
- Replace `SimpleGradientBoosting` → `sklearn.ensemble.GradientBoostingClassifier`
- Create a `ModelWrapper` class to provide a unified interface for all three models
- Retain the same `predict()`, `predict_proba()`, `feature_importances()` API so the GUI doesn't need to change
- Add `GridSearchCV` optimization for the best-performing model
- Add model serialization (`joblib.dump`/`joblib.load`) for saving/loading trained models

#### Expected Accuracy Improvements

| Model | Current (synthetic) | Expected (real data + sklearn) |
|-------|--------------------|---------------------------------|
| Logistic Regression | 71.87% | ~82-84% |
| Random Forest | 64.40% | ~84-86% |
| Gradient Boosting | 72.01% | ~86-87% |

